    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "A group of 5 adults and 3 children paid a total of $\\$108$ for their concert tickets.\nAnother group of 3 adults and 10 children paid $\\$155$.\nFind the cost of an adult ticket and the cost of a child’s ticket.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Adult ticket: $\\$15$; child’s ticket: $\\$11$.",
      "worked": "Let $a$ be the cost of an adult ticket and $c$ the cost of a child’s ticket, in dollars.\n$$\\begin{align*}5a+3c&=108 &&\\text{(1)}\\\\3a+10c&=155 &&\\text{(2)}\\end{align*}$$\nMultiply (1) by 10 and (2) by 3.\n$$\\begin{align*}50a+30c&=1080 &&\\text{(3)}\\\\9a+30c&=465 &&\\text{(4)}\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (4) from (3).\n$$\\begin{align*}41a&=615\\\\a&=15\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $a=15$ into (1).\n$$\\begin{align*}5(15)+3c&=108\\\\75+3c&=108\\\\3c&=33\\\\c&=11\\end{align*}$$\nAn adult ticket costs $\\$15$ and a child’s ticket costs $\\$11$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
